Example: Storing and Querying Vectors in SQL Server 2025
1. Create a Table with a Vector Column
SQL Server 2025 adds a VECTOR data type. You specify the dimension (e.g., 1536 for OpenAI embeddings).


CREATE TABLE Documents (
    Id INT PRIMARY KEY,
    Title NVARCHAR(200),
    Content NVARCHAR(MAX),
    Embedding VECTOR(1536)  -- store a 1536-dimensional vector
);


2. Insert Data with Embeddings
You can insert embeddings (arrays of floats) directly into the vector column.

INSERT INTO Documents (Id, Title, Content, Embedding)
VALUES (
    1,
    'AI Basics',
    'Introduction to artificial intelligence concepts.',
    VECTOR[0.0123, 0.2345, 0.5432, ...]  -- truncated example
);


Perform a Similarity Search
SQL Server 2025 provides functions like DOT_PRODUCT or COSINE_DISTANCE for vector similarity.

DECLARE @queryEmbedding VECTOR(1536) = VECTOR[0.0111, 0.2222, 0.3333, ...];

SELECT TOP 5 Id, Title, DOT_PRODUCT(Embedding, @queryEmbedding) AS Score
FROM Documents
ORDER BY Score DESC;


4. Create a Vector Index (Optional for Performance)
You can create a vector index to accelerate similarity searches:

CREATE VECTOR INDEX idx_embedding
ON Documents (Embedding)
WITH (DISTANCE = COSINE);


